11. RETRY AND OUTPUT VALIDATION

Implement server/providers/retry.ts.

Rules:

1. HTTP 429 and 5xx: retry with backoff, maximum two retries.
2. After retries fail, try configured fallback models from the same provider only.
3. Maximum three fallback models.
4. If all fail, return a clear Indonesian error.
5. Zod validation failure: one additional model attempt, then failed.
6. Truncated output: do not automatically retry. Return output_truncated with advice to increase max tokens.
7. All actual model calls count toward the daily limit.

Every provider response must pass Zod validation before it reaches the UI.

Never display malformed JSON as successful agent output.

Never silently repair an invalid response without running validation again.

JSON mode fallback

If a provider or model does not support json_schema:

1. Use json_object if supported.
2. Otherwise use prompt_only.
3. Always validate with Zod afterward.

Normalize schemas to the supported provider subset.

Use native Zod JSON Schema support when available. If not available in the installed version, use zod-to-json-schema.

